< bestmove {legal}
# UCI position after an unknown prefix replaces a position with one reply.
> position fen 7k/8/5K1Q/8/8/8/8/8 b - - 0 1
> go
# Rules 4, 5, 7 and 10. Black must play h8g8, then h6g7 is checkmate.
# Python-chess counts 1, 21, 30 and 730 nodes at plies 1 to 4.
< info depth 4 score mate -1 nodes 782
< bestmove h8g8
> \xff unknown position fen 7k/8/5K2/6Q1/8/8/8/8 b - - 0 1
> go
# Rules 4, 5, 7 and 10. Black must play h8h7, then g5g7 is checkmate.
# Python-chess counts 1, 25, 45 and 1228 nodes at plies 1 to 4.
< info depth 4 score mate -1 nodes 1299
< bestmove h8h7
# The ignored command consumes its arguments, including position.
> unknown setoption name Path value position fen 7k/8/5K1Q/8/8/8/8/8 b - - 0 1
> go
# Rules 4, 5, 7 and 10. Black must play h8h7, then g5g7 is checkmate.
# Python-chess counts 1, 25, 45 and 1228 nodes at plies 1 to 4.
< info depth 4 score mate -1 nodes 1299
< bestmove h8h7
> go
# Rules 4, 5, 7 and 10. Black must play h8h7, then g5g7 is checkmate.
# Python-chess counts 1, 25, 45 and 1228 nodes at plies 1 to 4.
< info depth 4 score mate -1 nodes 1299
# The reference follows the prefixed position and skips the setoption value.
< bestmove {legal}
# UCI quit.
> quit
! exit
